        "response": "I agree that it is a strong, mature candidate and that the proposed trio covers key stages of the invention and realization. I give the lattice clocks priority because their metrological performance provides a particularly direct and continuing route to precision tests of fundamental physics, with Katori and Ye also making complementary contributions."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "lindroth-eva",
        "point": "You argue that titanium-sapphire lasers and passive mode-locking made intense femtosecond pulses widely accessible, while noting that the medium and mode-locking advances have distinct histories.",
